Falsifies `system_tests::user::name_resolver_tests::a_forgotten_badge_is_denied_and_its_window_serves_the_next_client`.

Architecture: aarch64

The defect: a forget frees the badge's grant and deletes the resolver's capability to the client's
page, but never unmaps it. The window still holds the old client's page, so the next client granted
that window cannot map its own there, its page is deleted, and it can never resolve. Worse, the
resolver would keep reading and writing a page from a client that has ended.

Expected to fail: the second badge's first case answers `NOT_ATTACHED` (status 7) where the gate
wants `OK`. Measured 2026-10-12 (UTC) on aarch64: red with exactly that assertion.

